	"items": {
		"_help": "Grenade items (playtest 2026-10-22 #5, Skillz, DESIGN §25, /workspace/skillz/GRENADE_ITEMS_API.md). A grenade is a GearItem (GrenadeItem, class 'grenade') in the Inventory 'grenade' equip slot; the equipped one is what you throw (player.gd §25 hunk: GrenadeItem.resolve). Empty slot = the class grenade (PlayerClass.grenade_id). Grenade COUNT (charges, cooldown refill) stays on the player; the item only picks the type + rolled Fittings. Item rarity = the type's rarity (grenades[id].rarity, so Netz's variant/rarity check holds). item_power is rolled like other gear (loot_tables item_power); every damage key x (1 + (IP-100) x ip_damage_per_point), floor ip_mult_min. fittings_per_rarity = rolled Fittings (mods) per rarity; starter items (class grenade on a fresh / migrated stash) have starter_fittings. fittings: id -> {name, stat (what it multiplies), range [lo, hi] (rolled uniformly, rounded to 0.01), text ({pct} = the rolled % change), needs (optional: only on types whose base data has this key > 0), types (optional allow list)}. Groups of keys each stat touches: damage_keys, radius_keys, effect_keys[type]. heal_frac is capped at heal_frac_cap. Names are original (no third-party terms): the rolled parts are 'Fittings', the maker is the item's manufacturer.",
